---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="Quick start" current="/guides/quick-start/">
  <article class="doc">
    <header class="doc-header">
      <span class="eyebrow">Guide</span>
      <h1>Quick start</h1>
      <p class="lead">Initialize a config, validate your files, and choose the output format that matches your workflow.</p>
    </header>

    <h2>1. Create a config</h2>
    <pre><code>dollarlint init</code></pre>
    <p>The interactive setup writes a starter <code>.dollarlint.toml</code>. It will not overwrite an existing config unless you confirm it or pass <code>--force</code>.</p>

    <h2>2. Validate a directory</h2>
    <pre><code>dollarlint validate .</code></pre>
    <p>The validate command discovers supported file types, loads each declared schema, and prints grouped results.</p>

    <h2>3. Add locations when fixing issues</h2>
    <pre><code>dollarlint validate ./config --locations</code></pre>
    <p>Line and column positions make text and JSON output easier to use during local fixes.</p>

    <h2>4. Use machine-readable output in automation</h2>
    <pre><code>dollarlint validate . --json
dollarlint validate . --sarif &gt; dollarlint.sarif</code></pre>
  </article>
</DocsLayout>
